 "issue_title": "Bug: CSV boolean options accept None and integers as booleans",
 "issue_body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nBoolean options such as `has_header`, `trim_headers`, and `write_header` are assigned directly into pybind-backed config objects. Python values like `0`, `1`, and `None` are accepted as booleans instead of being rejected.\r\n\r\n## Evidence / audit context\r\n\r\n- Audit target: latest `origin/main` at `3ebc37cae0c2dc6a1b0d83c62eac468d83f1242f`.\r\n- Severity: **Low**.\r\n- Relevant paths: `arnio/io.py`, `bindings/bind_arnio.cpp`.\r\n- `read_csv(path, has_header=None)` behaved like `has_header=False`, and `write_csv(frame, path, write_header=0)` wrote no header.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nimport tempfile\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\nimport arnio as ar\r\n\r\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\r\n    path = Path(td) / \"input.csv\"\r\n    path.write_text(\"a,b\r\n1,2\r\n\")\r\n    print(ar.read_csv(path, has_header=None).columns)\r\n\r\n    frame = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1]}))\r\n    out = Path(td) / \"out.csv\"\r\n    ar.write_csv(frame, out, write_header=0)\r\n    print(out.read_text())\r\n```\r\n\r\nExpected: non-`bool` values should raise `TypeError`.\r\n\r\n## Why this matters\r\n\r\nThis can produce incorrect data, delayed runtime failures, or misleading API behavior. Arnio is a data preparation library, so silent corruption or unclear validation errors are especially risky for downstream pandas, sklearn, and data-quality workflows.\r\n\r\n## Suggested fix\r\n\r\nValidate boolean options in Python with `isinstance(value, bool)` before assigning to C++ config objects.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] `has_header`, `trim_headers`, and `write_header` reject `None`, `0`, `1`, strings, and other non-bool values.\r\n- [ ] Valid `True` and `False` behavior remains unchanged.\r\n- [ ] Tests cover read, scan, and write options where applicable.\r\n- [ ] Error messages name the invalid parameter.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nThis issue was created from a manual end-to-end audit and includes a minimal repro where applicable.\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/719",
