 "pr_title": "fix: validate boolean options in read_csv, write_csv, and scan_csv (#719)",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\nFixes #719\r\n\r\nBoolean options `has_header`, `trim_headers`, and `write_header` were silently accepting non-bool values like `None`, `0`, `1`, and strings instead of raising a `TypeError`.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Added `_validate_bool_option()` helper in `arnio/io.py`\r\n- Applied validation in `read_csv`, `read_csv_chunked`, and `write_csv`\r\n- Added tests in `tests/test_write_csv.py` and `tests/test_bool_validation_standalone.py`\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n- All 7 new tests pass\r\n- Valid `True` and `False` behavior unchanged\r\n- Error messages name the invalid parameter\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n- [x] `has_header`, `trim_headers`, and `write_header` reject `None`, `0`, `1`, and strings\r\n- [x] Valid `True` and `False` behavior remains unchanged\r\n- [x] Tests cover read, scan, and write options\r\n- [x] Error messages name the invalid parameter",
